#. vextrus/takeoff/messages/read_file.py (ticket 21a): the read job per file, its upload and its reading.
msgid "takeoff.read_file.not_read_in_full"
msgstr "{limit, select, sheets_capped {This file holds more sheets than Vextrus lists from one file, so some of its sheets are not in the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be listed.} layouts_not_read {This file holds more sheets than Vextrus lists from one file, so some of its layout tabs were not looked at and their sheets are not in the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be listed.} frames_capped {This file holds more sheet borders than Vextrus looks at in one file, so some of its sheets may be missing from the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be found.} walk_visit_limit {This drawing is larger than Vextrus looks through in one file, so some of its sheets may be missing from the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be found.} read_budget {This drawing is larger than Vextrus looks through in one file, so some of its sheets may be missing from the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be found.} texts_capped {This file holds more text than Vextrus reads from one file, so some sheet numbers or titles may be missing in Step 1. Check them there, or mark the file for Vextrus.} pair_budget {The title blocks in this file hold more writing than Vextrus reads, so some sheet numbers or titles may be missing in Step 1. Check them there, or mark the file for Vextrus.} frame_labels_capped {Some title blocks in this file hold more writing than Vextrus reads, so some sheet numbers or titles may be missing in Step 1. Check them there, or mark the file for Vextrus.} frame_values_capped {Some title blocks in this file hold more writing than Vextrus reads, so some sheet numbers or titles may be missing in Step 1. Check them there, or mark the file for Vextrus.} layout_frames_capped {Some layout tabs in this file show more sheet borders than Vextrus checks, so a sheet may be listed twice in Step 1, once from the drawing and once from its layout tab. Leave out the copy there, or mark the file for Vextrus.} viewport_budget {The layout tabs in this file hold more views than Vextrus checks, so some tabs that show nothing may be listed in Step 1 as sheets. Leave them out there, or mark the file for Vextrus.} layout_viewport_unknown_capped {Vextrus could not tell what many of this file's layout tabs show, more than it lists from one file, so some of them are not in the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be listed.} layout_blank_not_proposed {More than one layout tab in this file looks blank: Step 1 lists the first, to leave out, and not the others. If one of them is a sheet, mark the file for Vextrus.} register_headings_capped {A sheet in this file holds more drawing lists than Vextrus reads from one sheet, so some rows of its Drawing List may be missing and the check against it may be incomplete. Mark the file for Vextrus.} other {Vextrus stopped looking for sheets in this file partway ({limit}), so some of its sheets may be missing from the sheet list. Mark it for Vextrus so the rest can be found.}}"

msgid "takeoff.read_file.not_started"
msgstr "{file} was not added: Vextrus could not start reading it just now. Add it again in a minute, and tell Vextrus if this keeps happening."

msgid "takeoff.read_file.not_started_again"
msgstr "Vextrus could not start reading {file} just now. Add it again in a minute to start it, and tell Vextrus if this keeps happening."
